# oodac Compiler Core Functional Review — 2026-09-01 (v2.10.0 SSoT)
File: openOODA/audit/oodac_survey_2026_09_01.oot

Scope: 540 .oo/.oot files / 78,277 lines of the self-hosted single-pass compiler. Survey + first-principles fixes. No source deletions of legacy code paths (the codebase has already eliminated legacy compat layers per the no-compat-layer directive).

## 0. Surface Inventory

```
540 .oo + 1 .oot = 541 files
78,277 total lines (pre-fix) → 78,318 total lines (post-fix)
2,677 pub fn declarations
519 .oo in flat parent ooda/oodac/, 15 in ast/, 4 in types/
main.oo: 139 imports (highest-coupling entry)
```

## 1. 256-Line Cap Distribution (post-fix)

| Lines | Count | % | Risk |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :--- |
| 1-200 | 388 | 72% | safe |
| 201-250 | 110 | 20% | moderate |
| 251-254 | 21 | 4% | tight |
| 255 (1-line margin) | 10 | 2% | 1-line buffer for additions |
| 256 (at cap) | 10 | 2% | 0 buffer |

10 files at the 256-line cap risk. Refactoring each requires a per-subsystem deep-dive (e.g., extract helpers, decompose large switch dispatch). x86_phi_resolve.oo is at 255 (1-line margin), restorable to original 255 state.

## 2. First-Principles Fixes Applied (this turn)

